## FOLLOW-UP COMMIT (served-browser retest, orchestrator 2026-10-30)

SERVED RESULT was a PARTIAL FAIL: arm worked (Ballista * highlighted,
Defenses 0 / Green 300 — correct), but cycle+MouseLeft placed NOTHING,
RMB placed nothing (consistent with "nothing armed the place path").

### Root cause — NOT the G5 mechanism. TWO real web-path bugs + one
### misread. Reproduced headlessly with a REAL main.gd forwarder feed
### (godot/sim/g5_real_relay_probe.gd, synthesizing InputEventKey /
### InputEventMouseButton through main._unhandled_input + the JS
### _on_js_key entry), plus a served export of 19715d4 driven in a real
### browser on :8142 (frames g5x-hub.png / g5x-after-lmb.png).

1. WEB DOUBLE-FEED (REAL, fixed): on web ONE physical keypress reaches
   GWBridge.on_key TWICE — the shell's JS keydown/keyup relay (the path
   my direct-injection probe used) AND Godot's own canvas pipeline via
   main.gd _unhandled_input. Measured on 19715d4: one KeyM press placed
   TWO (spy showed the relay; the engine forwarder is the second feed).
   FIX: bridge.on_key EDGE-TRIGGERS the press queue (down ignored while
   the code is already held). held stays the level view; every shipped
   caller is down/up-paired. Coupled harness fix: mission_smoke_swap
   left F-keys held (never released), so the now-correct edge guard
   dropped its re-press — releases added (real keys always key-up);
   test_mission_smoke + test_hud 24 green beside it.
2. COMBAT-PHASE SILENT REFUSAL (REAL UX trap, fixed): the served retest
   ran AFTER the ~16s build window — its own coach copy ("FIGHT: both
   mouse buttons hit") is FIGHT-phase proof, so the build had ALREADY
   ENDED; place_id legitimately refuses with {why:phase}. But the panel
   rows stayed ENABLED through combat, so a press armed a row that could
   only answer phase-refusal — indistinguishable from "never armed".
   FIX: panel.sync disables picker rows whenever phase != build (W17e's
   ONE enabled pass) and cancels any armed aim on the lock.
3. MISREAD (no code): cycle/LMB/RMB DID work headlessly through the real
   forwarder; the browser frames g5x2-placed.png (placed, Green 200)
   confirm after fixes 1+2 removed the double-feed and the combat trap.

